{
  "dom_id": "step-q146340",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be discrete random variables with the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(1,4).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables with the joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\sum }_{{x}_{i}\\le x}{\\sum }_{{y}_{i}\\le y}f({x}_{i},{y}_{i}).\n$$\n\nBy definition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1,4) & =P(X\\le 1,Y\\le 4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe start by highlighting all cells in the table that correspond to $X\\le 1,Y\\le 4.$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1,4) & ={\\sum }_{x\\le 1}{\\sum }_{y\\le 4}f(x,y) \\\\  & =f(-1,2)+f(-1,4)+f(1,2)+f(1,4) \\\\  & =0.3+0.2+0.2+0.1 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
